  ],
  "sessions": [],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "When a human foregoes deliberation and adopts AI output as their own with minimal scrutiny.",
      "timestamp_sec": 134,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=134s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "For example, for questions where the AI was right, the human performance increased by 25 percentage points. Whereas when the AI was wrong, it decreased by 15.",
      "timestamp_sec": 134,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=134s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Most interestingly, they saw that 80% of participants were accepting those AI answers even when they were wrong.",
      "timestamp_sec": 191,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=191s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, for experiments, we wanted to answer the question, would a skilled reviewer catch a false alarm or would they just rubber stamp it?",
      "timestamp_sec": 296,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=296s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "despite the fact that our human reviewers are consistently scoring above 90% on their accuracy calibration metrics, they actually accepted 50% of these fake signals",
      "timestamp_sec": 375,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=375s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And this coin flip rate is something that is a strong suggestion of automation bias.",
      "timestamp_sec": 375,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=375s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "We knew that the problem was not the model. Our model has a 1% false positive rate, and also these were sessions that were negatively predicted.",
      "timestamp_sec": 423,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=423s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "First, the AI signal is just a preliminary alert. They're the final decision-maker.",
      "timestamp_sec": 461,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=461s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "This simple copy change led a 21% increase in rejection rates",
      "timestamp_sec": 461,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=461s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "As an AI engineer, your interaction loop determines how effective your AI system is and also what you can learn from it.",
      "timestamp_sec": 507,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=507s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "You can't really change the way a human behaves unless you are that human. But, what you can do is tweak that interaction such that it can elicit different results from that human behavior.",
      "timestamp_sec": 551,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=551s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Think of your structured interactions as a system property that specifically yields high-quality data.",
      "timestamp_sec": 596,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=596s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, over time, your model becomes more confident, and the human is not encouraged to think further.",
      "timestamp_sec": 639,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=639s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, they continue to defer to the AI, and the AI becomes the person in the driving seat.",
      "timestamp_sec": 684,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=684s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "That means that you have true positive and negative labels that are honest and get logged to then continue to have model improvements that are targeting exactly where the model goes wrong.",
      "timestamp_sec": 684,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=684s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "For example, if there's somebody who has a hearing aid, that means that the model correctly predicted that there are headphones or earbuds detected.",
      "timestamp_sec": 764,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=764s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Either way, in both of these cases, you're just becoming a rubber stamp.",
      "timestamp_sec": 966,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=966s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Instead, you probably want a coding agent that acts like a junior developer.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1005,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1005s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Lastly, for sustained attention, you want to build in friction exactly where the stakes are high.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1142,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1142s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "reframe your system to think of the human as investigator, not just a validator",
      "timestamp_sec": 1142,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1142s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Next principle is every interaction is already a label.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1270,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1270s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Another principle is to stop asking how to evaluate the model.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1361,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1361s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Sometimes the fix is not a better model or more oversight, it's just engineering the interaction itself.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1537,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1537s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "claim": "Expert human reviewers with >90% calibration accuracy will uphold roughly half of fabricated AI flags, so reviewer skill does not protect against automation bias.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 375,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=375s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rubber-stamping failure was caused by the interface, not by the model (1% false positive rate) or by insufficiently skilled proctors.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 423,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=423s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Changing only the guideline copy — framing the AI signal as preliminary and requiring independent evidence — shifted rejection rates 21% without any model or UI change.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 461,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=461s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "The human-in-the-loop process is cyclical, not linear: interaction design determines human behavior, which determines the training and eval data for the next model.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 551,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=551s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "You cannot change human behavior directly, so the only real lever an engineer has is the interaction.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 551,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=551s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Rubber-stamped approvals get logged as truth and make models spuriously more confident over time.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 639,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=639s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "A single yes/no CTA that conflates 'was the model's perception correct' with 'should we penalize this user' produces false labels and degrades the model.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 764,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=764s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "LLM writing feedback should be inline and anchored to specific spans rather than delivered as a long block that rewrites the user's passage.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 877,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=877s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Both dominant coding-agent patterns — one giant diff, or per-file approval prompts — reduce the developer to a rubber stamp and produce low-information accept/reject data.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 966,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=966s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Friction is desirable and should be deliberately added where stakes are high, and removed where oversight is low.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 1191,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1191s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Systems that record a yes/no decision but not the human's subsequent manual edit capture a false signal that pollutes datasets.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 1320,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1320s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Success metrics and required data should be defined before the system is built, rather than asking afterward how to evaluate the model.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 1361,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1361s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Thumbs up/down feedback is insufficient; explicit feedback must be collected at the right touch points with enough nuance to drive improvements.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 1478,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDqzWpwkSls&t=1478s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Adding more human oversight is not by itself a fix for AI system quality.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 1537,
      "talk_slug": "build-ai-systems-for-discernment-not-approval",
